></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1995025375-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1995025375</doc-number> <kind>A1</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1998042642-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1998042642</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEM</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSAWA HIDEYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMATO YO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSAWA, HIDEYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMATO, YO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSAWA HIDEYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMATO YO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSAWA, HIDEYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMATO, YO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A gas-generating agent composition for a pretentioner, characterized as comprising, as main components, a binder having good resistance to heat and an oxidizing agent, and optionally a neutralizing agent for chlorine.      The composition has good heat resistance and is easy to produce and , when used, gives a gas after combustion  having  less contents of CO and a chlorine-containing gas.          Accordingly, the composition can be used for improving the heat resistance of a gas-generating agent and reducing the amount of CO gas, and is easy to produce and, when required, can reduce the amount of a chlorine-containing gas.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition contenant une substance génératrice de gaz destinée à un dispositif de mise en tension. La composition se caractérise en ce qu'elle comprend, comme éléments principaux, un liant ayant une bonne résistance à la chaleur, un comburant et, éventuellement, un agent de neutralisation du chlore. Cette composition présente une bonne résistance à la chaleur; elle est facile à produire et, pendant l'utilisation, donne après combustion un gaz de teneur en CO réduite et un chlore gazeux. Par conséquent, la composition peut être utilisée pour améliorer la résistance à la chaleur d'une substance génératrice de gaz et pour réduire la quantité de gaz CO; elle est facile à produire et peut, au besoin, réduire la quantité d'un chlore gazeux.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>